# Never text-edit large Unity assets

Never write `Assets/WiloLake.unity` (~85 MB), `Assets/Environment/Terrain/WiloLake.asset`
(~17 MB), or any text asset over ~2 MB through file-edit tools. Agent writes cap near 8 MB,
so a rewrite truncates mid-YAML and Unity loads the fragment — terrain, lake, and folder
GameObjects vanish and orphaned children collapse to the scene root.

Change the scene via Unity MCP `Unity_RunCommand` instead: mutate through the editor API,
`result.RegisterObjectModification(obj)` before edits, then `EditorSceneManager.SaveScene`.
Reloading after an external change is `AssetDatabase.Refresh()` +
`EditorSceneManager.OpenScene(path, OpenSceneMode.Single)`; this often exceeds the MCP
timeout yet still completes, so re-query the root count before assuming failure.

Prefer C# field initializers over scene values for MonoBehaviour tuning.

Check `git diff --stat Assets/WiloLake.unity` before finishing. A huge line deletion means
truncation — `git checkout -- Assets/WiloLake.unity`, then reload the scene.
